{"author":{"id":"dec876858d28babbadcead4137861bf586626b8518cbce9c5f4fc52ac3b424b8"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1791649400,"nonce":"aQykYLFtOKwIgxlCLbT69tgr+S4=","title":"text_area rebuilds its content on every keystroke, click and drag","message":"`TextArea` is still a `Stateful\u003cTextFieldState\u003e` whose handlers mutate `TextAreaState` and call `refresh_stateful`, rebuilding the content each time: the state `text_input` was in before b4fa30772178cc0a1bf024106d39b01f07b7c43e (dba8d31).\n\nSame pattern as text_input:\n\n- a revision signal on `TextAreaState`, bumped wherever a handler now calls `refresh_stateful`, plus the node id stored at build (the focus queue and `focused_text_area_node_id` read `stateful_state` today);\n- the box look (bg, border, radius, outline) as one computed over `visual` with render bindings, border width as a layout binding;\n- scroll and caret as bound translates;\n- every computed read once at build, or it tracks no dependencies and never fires.\n\nWhat is new for multi-line: the line count changes as the user types, so the lines need a keyed `for_each` (or a region) rather than fixed runs, and a selection spans lines (per-line before / selected / after runs, or per-line selection rects).\n\nAlso: text_area still gets Stateful's auto POINTER_DOWN focus (662a528), and `clear_focused_text_area` in text_input.rs has no caller.\n\nRisks to test for: IME composition, wrapping, vertical scroll-into-view of the caret, mobile focus (`focus_text_area_deferred`), long-press selection.","files":null}]}